 record from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids February to March and October to November each came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those years. In 2025 the middle ran 207% of normal in April to May, then fell to 27% in November to December. So far in 2026 it sits at 34% in January to February and 79% in June to July. Grid 19654 has a preliminary estimate of 32.8 for August to September 2026.</p>"}
